```

But wait — the contextmenu and mousedown/touchstart listeners also leak on redraw (a new board element each time? no — renderWrap: does it replace the wrap's children or replace the wrap itself?). The bug report only mentions RO. The old board element is detached, so listeners on a detached element don't leak beyond the element itself. The RO is the issue because the global RO controller holds the element. Keep the fix scoped to RO only — minimal, fix the reported bug.

Actually, should bindBoard also handle disconnecting the previous RO? The issue says "on destroy and on redraw." If we store ro on state.dom, then on redraw the old state.dom.ro is orphaned (state.dom gets replaced) — so we have to explicitly disconnect the old one in redrawAll before replacing state.dom. That way bindBoard only needs to assign the new ro.

But what if someone calls bindBoard twice without replacing state.dom? Only redrawAll calls it. No problem.

Alternative: have bindBoard itself disconnect `s.dom.ro` (which might be stale from before the state.dom replacement? no, state.dom has already been replaced). So bindBoard can't see the old RO.

